tively final milestone, but it’s just one dimension of a lifelong process. So when you say “all this lifelong plasticity stuff is just minor tweaking,” you’re highlighting a valid distinction—the major maturational build is indeed complete. But I’d argue that the plastic changes that follow are not minor at all in terms of their impact on who you are and what your brain can do. They’re just a different, lifelong kind of development, one that you get to author yourself.
